          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-15 07:17:03.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 16:19:15.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Handle a connection ack in one critical section",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Handle a connection ack in one critical section\n\nThe ack handler checked the connection state under the connection\nlock, then dropped the lock before setting up the data QPs and\nactivating the connection. Two acks handled at the same time, e.g. a\nlate ack from an earlier connection attempt and the current one,\ncould both pass the check, and the second would leak the QP list or\nfree it while senders use it.\n\nHold the lock from the state check until the connection is active,\nas the connection request handler does.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nChange-Id: Ic38d266ac9928e1f1378963dcb8b3974fa871cf7\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
